---

IMPORTANT — SCOPE OF THIS LICENCE

This licence applies to the written documentation only.

The 512 constraint set — the seven invariants defining execution-time
legitimacy — is not owned by any person or entity. It cannot be
licensed because it is not ownable. It was discovered, not invented.
Physics and scale force it into existence regardless of whether any
specific documentation exists.

No person may claim copyright, patent, or proprietary rights over
the 512 constraint set itself.

Anyone may build systems that satisfy 512's properties. No permission
is required. No licence is needed. No attribution is required for
the constraint set — only for the written documentation in this
repository if reproduced.

---

DISTINCTION FROM CVS

The Cryptographic Verification Sidecar (CVS) is an invented witness
architecture maintained in a separate repository. CVS is released
under Apache License 2.0. The licensing distinction between 512
(discovered constraint, documentation CC BY 4.0) and CVS (invented
architecture, Apache 2.0) is intentional and architecturally
significant.

